---
// src/pages/legal/cookie-notice.astro
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Notice"
  description="How this website uses cookies and similar technologies, and how to control them."
  updated="[DATE TO BE SET AT LAUNCH]"
  intro="This site is built to be quiet. It uses as little tracking as possible."
>
  <h2>What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files a website can store in your browser. Similar
    technologies include local storage and pixels. They are used to remember settings, to
    keep a site secure, and sometimes to measure how a site is used.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site currently uses</h2>
  <p>
    This website is a static site. As currently built, it does not set advertising or
    cross-site tracking cookies, does not embed social media trackers, and does not load
    fonts from third-party servers — typefaces are served from our own domain.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider may set a small number of strictly necessary cookies for
    security, load balancing, and spam prevention on form submissions.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>[Needs review:</strong> confirm with the hosting provider which strictly
    necessary cookies are set, and list them in the table below with name, purpose, and
    duration.<strong>]</strong>
  </p>

  <h3>Cookie inventory</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>[Cookie name]</strong> — [purpose] — [duration] — strictly necessary</li>
    <li><strong>[Cookie name]</strong> — [purpose] — [duration] — strictly necessary</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If we add analytics</h2>
  <p>
    If we later add analytics or a giving platform, we will update this notice before or
    at the time those tools go live, name the provider, describe what is collected, and
    add a consent mechanism if one is required.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>[Needs legal review:</strong> if any non-essential cookies or analytics are
    introduced, determine whether a consent banner is required for the ministry’s
    audience and add it before launch.<strong>]</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Controlling cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete or block cookies through your browser settings. Blocking strictly
    necessary cookies may affect form submission or site security features. Most browsers
    also offer a “Do Not Track” signal; because there is no common standard for honoring
    it, this site does not respond to it differently.
  </p>

  <h2>More information</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/legal/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for how we handle the
    information you send us, or write to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
